PHP serialize

	the PHP serialize() function 

		To serialize an object into a string, you use the serialize() function:

			serialize(mixed $value): string

	The serialize() function returns a string that contains a byte-stream representation of the object.

		serialize(mixed $value): string

		The serialize() function returns a string that contains a byte-stream representation of the object


	Notice that the serialize() function only serializes the properties of the object, not the method.



The __sleep() magic method #


	The __sleep() method returns an array that contains property names that will be serialized.

The __serialize()

	
	The __serialize() method is similar to the __sleep() method:

However, the __serialize() method returns an associative array of key/value pairs representing the object’s serialized form


	Use the serialize() function to serialize an object into a string of byte-stream representation.

	Use the __sleep() or __serialize() method to implement the logic before serialization.


Php unserialize

	
	 how to use the PHP unserialize() function to convert a serialized string into an object.


	 If the unserialize() function cannot convert the serialized string ($data) into an object, it returns false with an E_NOTICE.



	 The __unserialize() magic method

	  public function __unserialize(): void
    {
        $this->open();
