	PHP anonymous classes

		An anonymous class is a class without a declared name.


		<?php

		$myObject = new class {
		    // ...
		};

		in this syntax, you place the class keyword after the new keyword. The $myObject is the instance of the anonymous class.

		Example,

		$logger = new class {
			    public function log(string $message): void
			    {
			        echo $message . '<br>';
			    }
			};

			$logger->log('Hello');
			Code language: PHP (php)

		-> Internally, PHP generates a name for the anonymous class. To get the generated name, you can use the get_class() 

